      "message": "This parameter guards against most of the code size increase for this feature.  The remaining increase is one instruction to load a small literal into an argument-passing register, per call to chipset_reset or chipset_force_shutdown (but not all of them).  An A/B test with the current compiler shows that glados is affected by 28 bytes.  We expect to gain at least 2 kB by improvements in codegen by switching to the coreboot sdk.\n\nTightest boards:\nzinger 1140 (no change)\nminimuffin 1148 (no change)\nglados 1912 -\u003e 1884 (28 bytes larger)",
